					</div>
				</div>
				
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
					<strong>How it works on wedding day:</strong> The couple cuts the top tier of the gorgeous display cake for photographers. After the first bite, catering servers whisk the display cake into the commercial kitchen, where they slice both the display cake and pre-frosted sheet cakes on clean cutting boards, plating identical slices with raspberry coulis or chocolate garnish. Guests receive the exact same flavor and texture without ever knowing the majority came from a flat sheet pan!
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 5: The Cake Cutting Fee Trap -->
			<section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--accent-red); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
					5. The Hidden Venue "Cake Cutting Fee" Trap ($1.50 to $4.50 / Slice)
				</h3>
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
					Before signing a contract with an outside custom bakery, always review your venue or caterer's outside vendor policy. Many venues impose a mandatory <strong>Cake Cutting & Plating Surcharge</strong> ranging from <strong>$1.50 to $4.50 per guest</strong>.
				</p>

				<div class="callout-box danger" style="background: #fef2f2; border: 2px solid #fecaca; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
					<strong style="color: #991b1b; font-size: 1.1rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
						⚠️ Real-World Financial Calculation:
					</strong>
					<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; color: #7f1d1d; line-height: 1.6;">
						For 150 guests, a $3.00/slice venue cutting fee adds <strong>$450.00 + 22% service charge + tax = $588.00</strong> to your final venue bill! That means an $800 bakery cake actually costs you <strong>$1,388.00 out of pocket</strong>.
					</p>
				</div>

				<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;">
					How to Legally Reduce or Waive Cake Cutting Fees:
				</h4>
				<ul class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-left: 1.5rem;">
					<li><strong>Opt for a Dessert Buffet / Cupcake Display:</strong> Venues usually waive the fee if servers do not have to portion slices (e.g. cupcakes, macarons, mini dessert jars, or self-serve sheet bars).</li>
					<li><strong>Negotiate Before Signing the Venue Contract:</strong> Ask your sales manager to waive the outside cake fee as a booking incentive during your initial tour.</li>
					<li><strong>Inquire About In-House Dessert Trade-Offs:</strong> If your catering package includes an unwanted in-house plated dessert (e.g. chocolate mousse), ask to substitute outside cake plating at no extra charge.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 6: Dietary Upcharges & Premium Fillings -->
			<section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
					6. Gourmet Fillings, Dietary Accommodations & Tasting Box Policies
				</h3>
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
					Standard cake quotes typically cover basic flavors (Vanilla Bean, Rich Chocolate, Lemon Chiffon) paired with traditional American or Swiss buttercream. When upgrading to specialty pastry elements, expect standard industry surcharges:
				</p>

				<ul class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
					<li><strong>Gluten-Free / Vegan / Nut-Free Accommodations:</strong> +$1.00 to +$2.50 per slice due to expensive almond/oat flour substitutes, specialized binding starches, and dedicated sterile sanitization protocols to prevent cross-contamination.</li>
					<li><strong>Gourmet Curds & Compotes:</strong> +$0.50 to +$1.00 per slice for passionfruit curd, fresh raspberry gelee, salted caramel drizzle, or espresso ganache.</li>
					<li><strong>Liqueur Soaks & Boozy Infusions:</strong> +$0.75 per slice for Grand Marnier, Amaretto, Bourbon, or Champagne simple syrup cake wash.</li>
					<li><strong>Tasting Box Policies:</strong> Wedding cake tasting boxes generally cost <strong>$30 to $60</strong> for 4 to 6 flavor pairings. The majority of independent bakeries will credit 100% of this fee toward your final balance if you book within 14 days.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 7: Temperature Physics & Transport -->
			<section style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: #dc2626; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
					7. The Summer Meltdown Threat: Temperature Physics & Delivery Logistics
				</h3>
				<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
					Real butter begins to soften at <strong>72°F (22°C)</strong> and completely melts into a liquid puddle at <strong>82°F (28°C)</strong>. Placing a 3-tier buttercream cake in an un-airconditioned tent, sunny outdoor terrace, or direct sunbeam for more than 20 minutes can cause catastrophic structural collapse.
				</p>

				<div style="background: #fffbeb; border: 2px solid #fde68a; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
					<strong style="color: #92400e; font-size: 1.05rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
						🛡️ Summer Cake Preservation Rules:
					</strong>
					<ol style="margin: 0 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #78350f; line-height: 1.7;">
						<li><strong>Opt for White Chocolate Ganache Under-Structure:</strong> Ganache sets significantly firmer than buttercream and resists humidity far better during warm outdoor receptions.</li>
						<li><strong>Keep in Venue Walk-In Cooler Until 45 Minutes Before Cutting:</strong> Display the cake inside the temperature-controlled dining hall, and only wheel it outdoors for immediate ceremonial photos if necessary.</li>
						<li><strong>Demand Climate-Controlled Transit:</strong> Ensure your baker transports the cake on nonslip leveling mats with active vehicle air conditioning turned to maximum cool.</li>
					</ol>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 8: FAQ Section -->
			<section style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
				<h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--fg-pencil); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
					8. Frequently Asked Questions About Wedding Cake Pricing
				</h3>

				<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
					
					<details style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; cursor: pointer;">
						<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
							How far in advance should we book our wedding cake baker?
						</summary>
						<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
							Most boutique wedding bakeries only accept 2 to 4 custom tiered cakes per weekend to maintain strict artistic quality. You should begin flavor tastings and reserve your date <strong>6 to 9 months prior to your wedding</strong> (or 9 to 12 months for peak autumn and spring wedding seasons).
						</p>
					</details>

					<details style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; cursor: pointer;">
						<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
							What happens to the top tier? (Freezer anniversary tradition vs. fresh replica)
						</summary>
						<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
							Historically, couples froze the top 6-inch tier for 1 year to eat on their first anniversary. However, freezer-burned cake often tastes stale and dry. Many modern bakeries now include a <strong>complimentary fresh 6-inch anniversary mini-cake</strong> on your 1-year anniversary, allowing all tiers to be served fresh to your wedding guests!
						</p>
					</details>

					<details style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; cursor: pointer;">
						<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
							How much should we tip the wedding cake baker and delivery driver?
						</summary>
						<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
							If the business owner baked and delivered the cake personally, tipping is optional but appreciated (a heartfelt review and $25–$50 cash tip for complex on-site floral styling). If a delivery driver or assistant handled transit and setup, a <strong>$15 to $30 cash tip</strong> in an envelope handed to them on-site is standard etiquette.
						</p>
					</details>

					<details style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; cursor: pointer;">
						<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
							Can we provide our own florist's fresh flowers for the cake?
						</summary>
						<p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.7;">
							Yes, but with strict safety precautions. Many common wedding flowers (such as hydrangeas, lilies of the valley, calla lilies, and eucalyptus) are mildly toxic or treated with heavy chemical pesticides. Your baker must wrap all stems in food-safe floral tape or insert them into plastic safety posy picks before inserting them into edible cake tiers.
						</p>
					</details>

				</div>
			</section>

		</article>

		<RelatedTools currentPath="/cake-pricing-calculator" category="food-beverage" />

	</main>

	<!-- Interactive Calculation Script -->
	<script is:inline>
		const presetSelect = document.getElementById('cake-preset');
		const servingsInput = document.getElementById('servings');
		const tiersSelect = document.getElementById('tiers');
		const ingredientInput = document.getElementById('ingredientCost');
		const tierSupplyInput = document.getElementById('tierSupplyCost');
		const laborHoursInput = document.getElementById('laborHours');
		const hourlyRateInput = document.getElementById('hourlyRate');
		const complexityInput = document.getElementById('complexity');
		const valComplexity = document.getElementById('val-complexity');

		const chkDelivery = document.getElementById('check-delivery');
		const deliveryBox = document.getElementById('delivery-inputs');
		const deliveryMilesInput = document.getElementById('deliveryMiles');
		const setupFeeInput = document.getElementById('setupFee');

		const resTotalPrice = document.getElementById('res-total-price');
		const resPricePerSlice = document.getElementById('res-price-per-slice');
		const resServingsLabel = document.getElementById('res-servings-label');
		const tierBadge = document.getElementById('tier-badge');

		const barMaterials = document.getElementById('bar-materials');
		const barLabor = document.getElementById('bar-labor');
		const barProfit = document.getElementById('bar-profit');
		const barDelivery = document.getElementById('bar-delivery');

		const resMaterialsTotal = document.getElementById('res-materials-total');
		const resLaborHoursLabel = document.getElementById('res-labor-hours-label');
		const resLaborTotal = document.getElementById('res-labor-total');
		const resProfitMarginPct = document.getElementById('res-profit-margin-pct');
		const resProfitDollars = document.getElementById('res-profit-dollars');
		const rowDeliveryFee = document.getElementById('row-delivery-fee');
		const resDeliveryTotal = document.getElementById('res-delivery-total');
		const resInvoiceTotal = document.getElementById('res-invoice-total');

		const btnPrint = document.getElementById('btn-print-cake-quote');
		const btnDoc = document.getElementById('btn-export-cake-doc');

		function calculateCakePricing() {
			const servings = parseInt(servingsInput.value, 10) || 1;
			const tiers = parseInt(tiersSelect.value, 10) || 1;
			const ingredients = parseFloat(ingredientInput.value) || 0;
			const hardware = parseFloat(tierSupplyInput.value) || 0;
			const laborHours = parseFloat(laborHoursInput.value) || 0;
			const hourlyRate = parseFloat(hourlyRateInput.value) || 0;
			const complexity = parseFloat(complexityInput.value) || 1.0;

			valComplexity.textContent = `${complexity.toFixed(1)}x`;
			tierBadge.textContent = `${tiers} ${tiers === 1 ? 'Tier' : 'Tiers'}`;
			resServingsLabel.textContent = `${servings} guest servings`;

			// Delivery Math
			let deliveryFee = 0;
			if (chkDelivery.checked) {
				deliveryBox.style.display = 'grid';
				rowDeliveryFee.style.display = 'flex';
				const miles = parseFloat(deliveryMilesInput.value) || 0;
				const setup = parseFloat(setupFeeInput.value) || 0;
				deliveryFee = (miles * 1.5) + setup;
				resDeliveryTotal.textContent = `$${deliveryFee.toFixed(2)}`;
			} else {
				deliveryBox.style.display = 'none';
				rowDeliveryFee.style.display = 'none';
				deliveryFee = 0;
			}

			// Core Cost Math
			const materialsCost = ingredients + hardware;
			const laborCost = laborHours * hourlyRate;
			const baseCost = materialsCost + laborCost;

			// Price with complexity markup
			const cakePrice = baseCost * complexity;
			const profitDollars = cakePrice - baseCost;
			const profitPct = cakePrice > 0 ? Math.round((profitDollars / cakePrice) * 100) : 0;
			const pricePerSlice = servings > 0 ? (cakePrice / servings) : 0;
			const finalInvoice = cakePrice + deliveryFee;

			// Update Text Displays
			resTotalPrice.textContent = `$${cakePrice.toFixed(2)}`;
			resPricePerSlice.textContent = `$${pricePerSlice.toFixed(2)}`;
			resMaterialsTotal.textContent = `$${materialsCost.toFixed(2)}`;
			resLaborHoursLabel.textContent = `${laborHours} hrs @ $${hourlyRate}/hr`;
			resLaborTotal.textContent = `$${laborCost.toFixed(2)}`;
			resProfitMarginPct.textContent = `${profitPct}%`;
			resProfitDollars.textContent = `$${profitDollars.toFixed(2)}`;
			resInvoiceTotal.textContent = `$${finalInvoice.toFixed(2)}`;

			// Update Financial Bar Graph
			if (finalInvoice > 0) {
				const matPct = (materialsCost / finalInvoice) * 100;
				const labPct = (laborCost / finalInvoice) * 100;
				const proPct = (profitDollars / finalInvoice) * 100;
				const delPct = (deliveryFee / finalInvoice) * 100;

				barMaterials.style.width = `${matPct}%`;
				barLabor.style.width = `${labPct}%`;
				barProfit.style.width = `${proPct}%`;
				barDelivery.style.width = `${delPct}%`;
			}
		}

		// Preset handler
		presetSelect.addEventListener('change', () => {
			const p = presetSelect.value;
			if (p === 'textured-buttercream') {
				complexityInput.value = 1.4;
				laborHoursInput.value = 10;
				ingredientInput.value = 85;
				tierSupplyInput.value = 45;
			} else if (p === 'semi-naked') {
				complexityInput.value = 1.1;
				laborHoursInput.value = 7;
				ingredientInput.value = 70;
				tierSupplyInput.value = 35;
			} else if (p === 'smooth-fondant') {
				complexityInput.value = 1.8;
				laborHoursInput.value = 14;
				ingredientInput.value = 120;
				tierSupplyInput.value = 55;
			} else if (p === 'sugar-art') {
				complexityInput.value = 2.5;
				laborHoursInput.value = 20;
				ingredientInput.value = 160;
				tierSupplyInput.value = 70;
			} else if (p === 'cutting-sheet') {
				complexityInput.value = 1.2;
				laborHoursInput.value = 8;
				ingredientInput.value = 75;
				tierSupplyInput.value = 30;
			}
			calculateCakePricing();
		});

		// Live Listeners
		[servingsInput, tiersSelect, ingredientInput, tierSupplyInput,
		 laborHoursInput, hourlyRateInput, complexityInput, chkDelivery,
		 deliveryMilesInput, setupFeeInput].forEach(elem => {
			elem.addEventListener('input', calculateCakePricing);
			elem.addEventListener('change', calculateCakePricing);
		});

		// Print Quote Handler
		btnPrint.addEventListener('click', () => {
			const printWindow = window.open('', '_blank');
			if (!printWindow) { window.print(); return; }
			printWindow.document.write(`
				<!DOCTYPE html>
				<html>
				<head>
					<title>Custom Wedding Cake Quote — Manage.Wedding</title>
					<style>
						@page { size: 8.5in 11in; margin: 0.5in; }
						body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: #1e293b; }
						h1 { font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 4px; color: #0f172a; }
						table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 15px; }
						th, td { border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
						th { background-color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: bold; }
						.total-row { font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; background-color: #fef3c7; }
					</style>
				</head>
				<body>
					<h1>Custom Wedding Cake Client Quote</h1>
					<p>Servings: ${servingsInput.value} | Tiers: ${tiersSelect.value} | Per-Slice: ${resPricePerSlice.textContent}</p>
					
					<table>
						<thead><tr><th>Line Item</th><th>Details</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr><td><strong>Cake Design & Creation</strong></td><td>${tiersSelect.value}-Tier Custom Decorated Cake (${servingsInput.value} Servings)</td><td>${resTotalPrice.textContent}</td></tr>
							<tr><td><strong>Raw Ingredients & Hardware</strong></td><td>Ingredients, boards, dowels, transport boxes</td><td>${resMaterialsTotal.textContent}</td></tr>
							<tr><td><strong>Professional Labor</strong></td><td>${resLaborHoursLabel.textContent}</td><td>${resLaborTotal.textContent}</td></tr>
							${chkDelivery.checked ? `<tr><td><strong>Delivery & Setup</strong></td><td>Roundtrip mileage + on-site placement</td><td>${resDeliveryTotal.textContent}</td></tr>` : ''}
							<tr class="total-row"><td>TOTAL CLIENT INVOICE</td><td>Price Per Slice: ${resPricePerSlice.textContent}</td><td>${resInvoiceTotal.textContent}</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
					<script>window.onload = function() { window.print(); };<\/script>
				</body></html>
			`);
			printWindow.document.close();
		});

		// Export Word Doc
		btnDoc.addEventListener('click', () => {
			const content = `
				<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
				<head><title>Custom Cake Invoice</title>
				<style>body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; } table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; } th, td { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 8px; }</style>
				</head>
				<body>
					<h2>Custom Wedding Cake Invoice Quote</h2>
					<p>Servings: ${servingsInput.value} | Tiers: ${tiersSelect.value} | Price Per Slice: ${resPricePerSlice.textContent}</p>
					<table>
						<thead><tr><th>Line Item</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr><td>Base Cake (Ingredients + Labor + Margin)</td><td>${resTotalPrice.textContent}</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Delivery & Setup</td><td>${resDeliveryTotal.textContent}</td></tr>
							<tr><td><strong>TOTAL INVOICE</strong></td><td><strong>${resInvoiceTotal.textContent}</strong></td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</body></html>
			`;
			const blob = new Blob([content], { type: 'application/msword' });
			const link = document.createElement('a');
			link.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
			link.download = 'wedding-cake-quote.doc';
			link.click();
		});

		// Initial Run
		calculateCakePricing();
	</script>
</Layout>
